      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define intraclass correlation as a “statistical measure used to show how closely scores from different raters or scoring methods agree.”",
        "The packet only states that “intraclass correlation coefficients” were used in quantitative analyses to assess “reliability and bias,” but it does not explicitly support the wording about “how closely scores … agree” or that it applies broadly to “different scoring methods.”",
        "The second sentence is only partially supported: the packet supports that ICCs were used to assess reliability in the AI vs human rater pronunciation-rating context, but it does not explicitly state that ICCs were used specifically “to judge the reliability” in the exact terms given."
